x86_64-linux  one recorded rule, docs/CONFORMANCE.md "An inline member function is a strong symbol": every constructor and destructor here is inline, so clang writes only the form a use asks for and cxx1 writes both of Itanium's - the C1 and D1 forms are cxx1's extras and nothing else differs. The Windows comparison has one name per constructor and destructor and agrees on all thirty-four, which is the half that checks which constructor each member reaches
arm64-darwin  same rule: B's C1 is cxx1's extra and every name clang writes agrees
x86_64-windows  cxx1's element loop `__cxx1_vec_del_1M`, which the pad of a partly built array member calls since [except.ctor]/3 landed (2026-10-20), against clang's inline code - a file-local helper, once per class.
